{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CecPXAA6LdMnp6CeMRSNj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All rework is committed and verified. The only remaining item is an untracked telemetry log from a prior session (a generated artifact, not part of this rework — left alone).\n\n## Summary\n\nREVIEW-A (005) returned CHANGES-REQUESTED on WI-552 with three findings. All are fixed, tested, and the full suite is green.\n\n**MAJOR — cancelled-close refusal gap.** The refusal invariant gated on `brief == \"disposition\"`, but a CANCELLED close mints a **brief-less** adjudication row, so a cancelled close that queued no successor archived/merged silently — contradicting OI-73, Done-when 3, and the shipped contract text.\n\nThe key subtlety I found while fixing it: the reviewer's first suggestion (a `specref`-based outcome signal) *doesn't survive* — `_adjudication_close_text` **clears specref** at close, and the merge-side guard is the **primary** enforcement for cancelled, because a cancelled row is dispatched as an ordinary worker that **self-closes past `close_adjudication`** (`dispatch._close_done_adjudication` short-circuits on a finished branch). By merge time specref is gone. So I used the one signal that both survives the close *and* distinguishes the arms: the kit-generated **`dispose:` title prefix**, read by a single-sourced `intake.owes_successor(meta)` + `_DISPOSITION_TITLE_PREFIX` (both title builders now reference the constant). Both guards refuse when the row owes a successor and none was drafted; the spot-check, amendment, and census rows don't carry the prefix and owe none. `test_intake` models the real self-close with **specref cleared**; `test_handback` covers the close-side; plus a does-not-over-fire control.\n\n**MINOR — scheduler/validator disagreement.** `schedule._waiting_reasons` now emits `waiting:hard-pred-partial` alongside `waiting:hard-pred-cancelled`, so `--explain` agrees with the validator's `dead_dependency_findings` (which flags cancelled AND partial). Test added.\n\n**MINOR — stale comment.** Dropped the contradictory \"or the row simply gone … satisfies the edge\" clause from the `_OI_PENDING` comment; it now matches `_oi_satisfied` (a gone/absent OI fails closed).\n\n**Verification:**\n- `check.py --jobs 0`: PASS\n- smoke tier: 1430 passed / 8 skipped, 22.6s vs 60s budget\n- full unfiltered suite: **3202 passed, 24 skipped in 637.94s (10:37)**\n- `intake.py` module-size baseline re-stamped 1176 → 1179 (reviewed bump, reason in log)\n\nThe spec was already archived to `complete/` from the prior close (Deliverable before Context, specref cleared) and my rework didn't alter it, so the close ritual stands. No spine rows touched → no approval brief owed. Final commit `9286104a` carries the `WI: WI-552` trailer."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":362,"cache_read_input_tokens":160772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":362},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7faad0a5-6f7e-4143-90db-719aab8c792d","uuid":"a2f24683-6553-4918-a9dc-2b9139105ca5","request_id":"req_011CecPX947eH13Kyan63MNP"}
